# {{ project_name }}

This repository packages one Codex personal local marketplace into a Python
distribution. It starts without marketplace payload data.

## Build a marketplace payload

Build one router plugin from a source repository and embed its assembled
marketplace payload:

```sh
poetry run python scripts/build_marketplace.py \
  --repository-root ../werner-mcp-tools \
  --invocation ../werner-mcp-tools/router-plugin-config.json \
  --marketplace-name werner-mcp-tools
```

The resulting `resources/.agents/plugins/marketplace.json`, generated plugin,
and assembly receipt are the complete release payload. Build and install the
distribution, then run:

```sh
{{ project_slug }} [--dry-run] [--force] [--json] [--verbose]
```

Use `--force` only to replace a changed plugin with the embedded plugin. The
build script never reads a configured marketplace or `~/.codex`.
